{
  "0": "Across all four datasets, change only causal interest pooling from 0.8*h_t+0.2*m_t with half-life 4 to 0.9*h_t+0.1*m_t with half-life 2. Broader pooling regressed; this tests whether a smaller, more recent interest contribution preserves the incumbent benefit. Exclude padding and future states, retain final-real-position inference, and synchronize predictor metadata. Preserve truncation, embeddings, GRU topology, scoring, loss and optimizer.",
  "1": "Across all four datasets, increase the pointwise logistic coefficient from 0.2 to 0.4 while retaining the existing pairwise softplus term and uniform averaging over nonpadding targets. Stronger absolute-score supervision may improve separation without the recency weighting that regressed. Change only the loss coefficient; preserve sampling, embeddings, GRU topology, readout, scoring, optimizer and training settings.",
  "2": "Across all four datasets, add a deterministic prefix-length feature by multiplying each history embedding by 1+0.1*(1-exp(-k/8)), where k counts observed nonpadding interactions through that position within the retained history. This mildly distinguishes short-context inputs from established histories without relying on nonexistent repeats. Use identical causal computation during training and prediction; keep padding zero, candidate embeddings unchanged, and preserve learned embedding design, GRU topology, readout, loss and optimizer.",
  "3": "Across all four datasets, retain the shared 128-dimensional item table but replace strict unit normalization with e_i=(0.75+0.5*sigmoid(a_i))*normalize(v_i), using one jointly trained scalar a_i per item initialized to zero. Bounded learned norms may capture item-specific confidence while preserving tied input/output representations, unlike the regressed untied tables. Keep padding zero and preserve features, GRU topology, history policy, readout, dot-product scoring, loss and optimizer. Update the predictor writer to load matching checkpoints."
}
